# Normalize every text file to LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# THIS IS LOAD-BEARING, not a style preference. Several guards in test/ read their own
# source tree as TEXT and match against literal "\n":
#
#   - test/engine-purity.test.js's stripComments() splits on "\n" and then strips
#     /\/\/.*$/ per line. Under CRLF the trailing "\r" makes "$" miss, so NOTHING is
#     stripped and the DOM/nondeterminism scan reads live code out of prose comments —
#     the word "window" in "the brief banking window" fails the purity guard.
#   - test/types-contract.test.js anchors on `@typedef {Object} <Name>\n`. Under CRLF that
#     never matches, so five typedef-drift guards fail OPEN — the worst direction for a
#     guard to fail, and exactly the "green build nobody reads" problem the CI workflow's
#     own pinned-compiler comment warns about.
#
# Both were real: with git's core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) and no file here,
# `npm test` reported 13 spurious failures on a tree that is green on Linux CI. Fixing the
# guards to tolerate CRLF is necessary but not sufficient — a repo whose tests read their
# own source is far easier to reason about when the bytes on disk match the bytes in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched by the normalization above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.wav binary
